WEBVTT

00:00:01.246 --> 00:00:03.874
You met a girl! Yes! Tell me everything.

00:00:03.874 --> 00:00:06.376
What's her name? Mary? Scarlett? Josephine?

00:00:06.376 --> 00:00:08.128
Barnabas. Terrific.

00:00:08.128 --> 00:00:11.006
No, he's an old friend of Dad's. Wonderful.

00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:14.134
No! He's a thief. Oh.

00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:17.178
Peter, you do not have my blessing to kiss a thief.

00:00:17.178 --> 00:00:19.473
Ugh, would you just let me tell you my story?

00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:20.641
[LAUGHING]

00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:21.850
Race you, Flopsy.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.269
I am not Flopsy anymore. Hm?

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:28.148
I've changed my name to be even different-er than you.

00:00:28.148 --> 00:00:31.151
From now on, I'm Lavatory.

00:00:31.151 --> 00:00:33.236
Lavatory? Yes.

00:00:33.236 --> 00:00:36.197
And I run on two legs now.

00:00:36.197 --> 00:00:37.324
It's classier.

00:00:37.324 --> 00:00:39.034
[GRUNTING SOFTLY]

00:00:39.034 --> 00:00:41.954
BEA: Think how much of this land we'll be able to preserve.

00:00:41.954 --> 00:00:44.915
All the nature our children will be able to explore.

00:00:44.915 --> 00:00:47.626
Check it out, sisters. Ah! Wait for me!

00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:49.210
[BOTH GRUNTING]

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.504
[LAUGHING]

00:00:50.504 --> 00:00:52.547
THOMAS: I never had a chance to do that.

00:00:52.547 --> 00:00:56.217
Not much frolicking in the orphanage.

00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:59.220
Which is why I also picture having some two-legged children

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.639
to frolic with.

00:01:00.639 --> 00:01:02.975
Yeah, and they'd have that whole mountain

00:01:02.975 --> 00:01:04.893
if I painted the rabbits in high-tops.

00:01:04.893 --> 00:01:06.227
THOMAS: And the whole valley

00:01:06.227 --> 00:01:08.105
if you put them in T-shirts and jeans.

00:01:08.105 --> 00:01:10.565
BEA: Yeah. Can you imagine?

00:01:10.565 --> 00:01:13.527
What's going on with her? Changed her name to "Bathroom."

00:01:13.527 --> 00:01:14.569
Huh?

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:16.488
[GRUNTS, YELLS]

00:01:16.488 --> 00:01:18.699
Aw.

00:01:18.699 --> 00:01:21.242
Go on. Join them. Frolic.

00:01:21.242 --> 00:01:22.536
Really? Yeah.

00:01:22.536 --> 00:01:24.496
THOMAS: Like, lie down horizontally,

00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:26.498
extend my legs, tuck in my arms,

00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:28.834
and roll down the hill safely and slowly?

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.919
Yes, I could-- Perhaps it's not for you.

00:01:30.919 --> 00:01:32.379
Let's go have a cup of tea.

00:01:32.379 --> 00:01:34.756
What do you mean, it's not for me? It is for me.

00:01:34.756 --> 00:01:36.299
No? It is most assuredly for me.

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:37.926
I can frolic. Don't think I can?

00:01:37.926 --> 00:01:39.887
I didn't say that. Madam, watch this.

00:01:39.887 --> 00:01:41.388
Imagine me, right,

00:01:41.388 --> 00:01:43.682
and our future children frolicking.

00:01:43.682 --> 00:01:47.019
Mm-hm. All right? Watch.

00:01:47.019 --> 00:01:50.022
Hey. See? Look, I'm frolicking.

00:01:50.022 --> 00:01:51.398
Oh.

00:01:51.398 --> 00:01:53.441
Whee!

00:01:53.441 --> 00:01:54.609
[ALL GASP]

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:55.944
I'm speeding up a little.

00:01:55.944 --> 00:01:58.739
I'm speeding up quite a bit. Ow! Oh! Oh!

00:01:58.739 --> 00:02:00.323
[SCREAMING]

00:02:00.323 --> 00:02:03.410
Help! Help!

00:02:05.662 --> 00:02:09.166
And that's why adults shouldn't do kid stuff.

00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:11.376
[SCREAMING]

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.964
I've been stealing from this garden my whole life

00:02:15.964 --> 00:02:17.591
and I was told I was wrong.

00:02:17.591 --> 00:02:18.884
But now with Barnabas,

00:02:18.884 --> 00:02:21.136
I know this is what I'm supposed to do.

00:02:21.136 --> 00:02:23.097
I'm supposed to be bad.

00:02:23.097 --> 00:02:25.348
This Barnabas sounds a bit dodgy.

00:02:25.348 --> 00:02:29.561
No, he's not dodgy. He gets me, like Dad did.

00:02:29.561 --> 00:02:32.189
And unlike him. Stay out of trouble.

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:35.442
See? He's had it out for me since the day he got here.

00:02:35.442 --> 00:02:38.319
He didn't say that to you. It was to all of us.

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:40.906
I'm talking to you, Peter, specifically.

00:02:40.906 --> 00:02:43.533
Stay out of trouble.

00:02:43.533 --> 00:02:46.536
And, anyway, our days are numbered here.

00:02:46.536 --> 00:02:47.871
You heard him today.

00:02:47.871 --> 00:02:50.249
As soon as they have a baby, we're done for.

00:02:50.249 --> 00:02:53.501
Did you feel any less loved when the girls were born?

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:56.838
It's different now. All they think I am is naughty.

00:02:56.838 --> 00:02:58.423
So I've embraced it.

00:02:58.423 --> 00:02:59.466
[SIGHS] [CAT YOWLS]

00:02:59.466 --> 00:03:01.051
Look, Barnabas has a big job

00:03:01.051 --> 00:03:03.386
that we can help with and set us up for life

00:03:03.386 --> 00:03:05.222
without having to rely on them.

00:03:05.222 --> 00:03:07.057
I don't know. Come on, girls.

00:03:07.057 --> 00:03:08.433
We're going to Gloucester.

00:03:08.433 --> 00:03:10.477
Okay. Why not? You're going to Gloucester?

00:03:10.477 --> 00:03:12.646
I'm running there tomorrow for cardio day.

00:03:12.646 --> 00:03:15.857
Today's chest and arms. Come on, fox, keep going!

00:03:15.857 --> 00:03:18.568
You've got this. Ugh, my trainer.

00:03:18.568 --> 00:03:20.779
Do I really need one? Probably not.

00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:24.950
Would I work out as hard without one? Probably not.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.410
♪ I need help ♪

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.037
[TRAIN HORN BLOWS]

00:03:29.037 --> 00:03:30.622
♪ I need help ♪

00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:32.249
[CLANGING]

00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:35.543
[YELLING] [WHOOPS]

00:03:36.628 --> 00:03:38.713
[PETER WHOOPS] [GROANING]

00:03:40.381 --> 00:03:43.218
[ALL PANTING]

00:03:43.218 --> 00:03:44.303
[GROANING]

00:03:45.887 --> 00:03:50.309
SQUIRREL: ♪ I'm asking you, please A little help ♪

00:03:50.309 --> 00:03:54.188
♪ Tell me you'll be there When I need somebody else ♪

00:03:54.188 --> 00:03:56.606
How do you always know what's going on with me?

00:03:56.606 --> 00:03:57.858
Just lucky, I guess.

00:03:57.858 --> 00:04:00.152
♪ I need help ♪

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.072
♪ I need help ♪

00:04:04.072 --> 00:04:05.615
[ALL PANTING]

00:04:05.615 --> 00:04:06.992
♪ I need help ♪

00:04:06.992 --> 00:04:08.535
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

00:04:08.535 --> 00:04:10.620
I brought some more just like me.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:14.166
Not all just like him. I have some reservations.

00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:16.084
SQUIRREL: ♪ I need help ♪

00:04:16.084 --> 00:04:18.419
Well, look at you lot. You've gotten so big.

00:04:18.419 --> 00:04:20.964
Last time I saw you, you were all babies.

00:04:20.964 --> 00:04:22.299
Benjamin, Cotton-Tail,

00:04:22.299 --> 00:04:24.759
Flopsy, Mopsy. BOTH: Yes!

00:04:24.759 --> 00:04:28.055
Well, it's "Lavatory" now, but formerly, yes.

00:04:28.055 --> 00:04:30.974
We're here to help on that big job you were talking about.

00:04:30.974 --> 00:04:33.143
Oh, no, no, no. It's much too dangerous.

00:04:33.143 --> 00:04:34.895
Okay, well, thanks for your time.

00:04:34.895 --> 00:04:37.147
Is there a taxi stand nearby?

00:04:37.147 --> 00:04:38.773
[WHISTLING]

00:04:38.773 --> 00:04:40.692
No, trust me. We used to steal

00:04:40.692 --> 00:04:42.652
from McGregor's garden all the time.

00:04:42.652 --> 00:04:45.364
This is much more different. I'll never forgive meself

00:04:45.364 --> 00:04:46.990
if anything happened to you. No.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.909
We can do anything you need. Right?

00:04:48.909 --> 00:04:51.870
If you need to get to a high place, we're your team.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:55.582
If you need us to be sneaky, we can be invisible.

00:04:55.582 --> 00:04:57.458
And if you need a distraction...

00:04:57.458 --> 00:05:01.004
ALL: ♪ Down by the bay Where the watermelons grow ♪

00:05:01.004 --> 00:05:04.507
♪ Back to my home I dare not go ♪

00:05:04.507 --> 00:05:08.511
♪ For if I do My mother will say: ♪

00:05:08.511 --> 00:05:11.181
♪ "Did you ever see a goose Kissing a moose?" ♪

00:05:11.181 --> 00:05:12.766
Are these yours?

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.562
♪ Down by the bay ♪

00:05:17.562 --> 00:05:19.731
[BEA & CUSTOMERS CHATTERING]

00:05:24.278 --> 00:05:26.863
[SHOP BELL JINGLES]

00:05:26.863 --> 00:05:28.573
And he's handy too.

00:05:28.573 --> 00:05:30.449
Is there anything this man can't do?

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:31.868
Ah, it's just a quick fix.

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:34.079
BEA: Thomas, can I call the glass man now?

00:05:34.079 --> 00:05:36.373
You've been at it for six hours.

00:05:36.373 --> 00:05:38.750
[TOY TRAIN HORN BLOWS]

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.962
Bea, Nigel Basil-Jones is here.

00:05:41.962 --> 00:05:44.005
Mr. Basil-Jones, what a nice surprise.

00:05:44.005 --> 00:05:46.383
Ha-ha-ha, there's my star.

00:05:46.383 --> 00:05:49.468
Is this a good time? "It's the best of times.

00:05:49.468 --> 00:05:51.096
It's the worst of times."

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.765
Dickens.

00:05:53.765 --> 00:05:55.642
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

00:05:55.642 --> 00:05:57.978
I couldn't wait to show you this.

00:05:57.978 --> 00:05:59.604
Ah! Oh, my goodness.

00:05:59.604 --> 00:06:01.273
THOMAS: That's incredible. Beautiful.

00:06:01.273 --> 00:06:03.275
We've had a tremendous early response,

00:06:03.275 --> 00:06:06.194
and interest in your next book is already through the roof.

00:06:06.194 --> 00:06:08.738
BEA: It's extraordinary. Huh.

00:06:08.738 --> 00:06:11.450
I have something for you too. Ah.

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:15.412
You can barely tell the difference.

00:06:15.412 --> 00:06:16.913
You did it. It's brilliant.

00:06:16.913 --> 00:06:21.042
Artistic, authentic, uncompromising.

00:06:21.042 --> 00:06:23.420
Where is that? It's in our garden.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.214
Mm, a bit limited in scope, no? It's where they live.

00:06:26.214 --> 00:06:28.633
I'm just thinking, now that you've made changes,

00:06:28.633 --> 00:06:31.510
you may want to expand it a bit, make it more fun, exotic.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:34.431
Maybe put them on a beach, give them surfboards,

00:06:34.431 --> 00:06:37.558
those little baby guitars. Ukuleles?

00:06:37.558 --> 00:06:39.560
Yes! Great idea. You see? Ha-ha!

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.647
You take my silly suggestions and make them so much better.

00:06:42.647 --> 00:06:43.773
Genius!

00:06:43.773 --> 00:06:45.733
They don't play ukuleles though.

00:06:45.733 --> 00:06:48.778
And they don't go to the beach. Right? I mean, they're rabbits.

00:06:48.778 --> 00:06:50.947
Why can't they be rabbits on the beach?

00:06:50.947 --> 00:06:54.034
Or a boat? Or a spaceship? A spaceship?

00:06:54.034 --> 00:06:58.163
Readers just want to be transported, Thomas.

00:06:58.163 --> 00:06:59.664
Dickens.

